# Story 81: Slack Channel (45s)
# Hook: Drop your humanoid into Slack and let it answer threads on its own.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-081-slack-channel.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Drop your humanoid into Slack and let it answer threads on its own.

[00:03.0 --> 00:10.0]
Launch rysh. The Slack channel is configured under contacts.slack: a bot token, an app token, and the channels to join.

[00:10.0 --> 00:20.0]
Tokens use the ENV_VAR syntax so they never sit in plaintext. Channels list the rooms the humanoid listens and replies in.

[00:20.0 --> 00:28.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode and spawn it from the file.

[00:28.0 --> 00:36.0]
Start the Slack adapter explicitly with ##humanoid channel start, the humanoid's name, and the channel type slack.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
##humanoid channels support shows the connection details -- which channels it joined and whether the adapter is live.

